},{"id":"B174-61","when":"June 1970","p":36,"h":"SPOTLIGHT ON ............ The Wilson Brothers","note":"scoring member of Belgrave's 2nd team, Open 50Kms. at Eastleigh 1949"},{"id":"B176-46","when":"December 1970","p":33,"h":"FROM 'The Belgravian' 25 years ago and 40 years ago","note":"10th, 5:08:01"},{"id":"B178-12","when":"September 1972","p":8,"h":"OBITUARY H.G.(\"HARRY\") CHURCHER.","note":"2nd in R.W.A. 10 miles Championship 1947, winning team"},{"id":"B180-65","when":"March 1973","p":38,"h":"FROM THE BELGRAVIAN 25 years ago ...... and 40 years ago","note":"1947: 2nd in 10 miles National walking championship"},{"id":"B197-30","when":"October 1978","p":22,"h":"The R.W.A. 10","note":"2nd National 10 miles walk 1947; 20th 1948"},{"id":"B212-25","when":"April 1988","p":21,"h":"& 50 years ago .... FEBRUARY 1938 - Our \"Open\" Walk","note":"19th"},{"id":"B229-16","when":"February 2001","p":8,"h":"Don E. Brown 1911-2000","note":"possibly in the photo"},{"id":"B229-20","when":"February 2001","p":11,"h":"J.E.C. Rutland"},{"id":"B253-12","when":"February 2007","p":4,"h":"From the Belgravian","note":"walker, 1947"},{"id":"B264-08","when":"No. 264","p":5,"h":"PERCY WRIGHT 1914-2008","note":"the late; persuaded the Army to include walking in sports events"}],"wrote":[{"id":"B156-27","when":"August 1965","p":15,"h":"HOW I TRAINED"}],"photos":[{"f":"crops/B229/B229-p08-walk-match-battersea-1938.jpg","c":"The caption that goes with this photograph in our archives reads:\n\"Walk Match at Battersea circa 1938. Starters include H.G. Churcher, C.E.Churcher, D.E. Brown, A.A.Harley, F. Jarvis, C.W.Redgrave.\"\nOur first stab at actually naming the faces came up with Don Brown (1), Harry Churcher (7), Charlie Churcher (23), C.W. Redgrave (24) and Alf Harley (behind Brown). However, as others have become involved and have cast their eyes over the picture, we are now not at all sure of anyone except Alf Harley. For instance, we are told that Charlie Churcher did not wear glasses and the chap next to Harry, second from the left, may be Jack Rutland If any reader can help us with more specific details of the race then we would be very pleased to hear from them.","id":"B229-16","w":"February 2001"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B229/B229-p08-walk-match-battersea-1938.jpg","caption":"The caption that goes with this photograph in our archives reads:\n\"Walk Match at Battersea circa 1938. Starters include H.G. Churcher, C.E.Churcher, D.E. Brown, A.A.Harley, F. Jarvis, C.W.Redgrave.\"\nOur first stab at actually naming the faces came up with Don Brown (1), Harry Churcher (7), Charlie Churcher (23), C.W. Redgrave (24) and Alf Harley (behind Brown). However, as others have become involved and have cast their eyes over the picture, we are now not at all sure of anyone except Alf Harley. For instance, we are told that Charlie Churcher did not wear glasses and the chap next to Harry, second from the left, may be Jack Rutland If any reader can help us with more specific details of the race then we would be very pleased to hear from them.","source":"B229-16","when":"February 2001"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Jack Rutland in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1933–2007: 214 mentions in 65 issues, 150 race results and 1 photograph. Wrote or reported 1 item.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B229/B229-p08-walk-match-battersea-1938.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-jack-rutland.html"},"legend":false}